<h2>Information We Use</h2>
<p>Toinky uses your email address, password hash, display name, optional profile photo, account roles, sign-in and verification records, preferences, friend relationships, invitations, games, choices, ratings, reviews, authored stories, media, and purchase/occasion records to operate the service. Your display name and profile photo can be visible to other players. Your story character and private character information are different from your account identity.</p>
<p>We use security counters derived from account or IP identifiers, account-security events, delivery records, and operational logs to protect accounts and investigate problems. Hashing an identifier does not necessarily make it anonymous. Passwords and authentication tokens are not included in account downloads.</p>
<p>Signed-in session records contain a hashed session identifier, browser/device description from the browser's user-agent header, activity and expiry times, second-factor status and password-confirmation time. Authenticator setup stores an encrypted secret, verification counter and hashed single-use recovery codes. We do not include session identifiers, authenticator secrets or recovery-code hashes in downloads. An unconfirmed authenticator setup expires after fifteen minutes.</p>
<h2>Age And Registration</h2>
<p>The minimum registration age is <?= (int)$privacyConfig['minimum_age']?>. Registration begins with a neutral birth-date check before requesting account details. The application retains a short eligibility decision, not the date of birth or exact age. A refusal uses a short essential cookie to discourage repeated attempts. If you believe a child has supplied personal information, contact us.</p>
<h2>AI And Other Providers</h2>
<p>Inky and optional AI features send selected story context and prompts to the operator-configured AI service through its authenticated gateway. Free-text stories or prompts can contain personal information; avoid including information about real people without an appropriate basis. AI requests and generated results may be logged for troubleshooting. AI is optional for story-engine operation.</p>
<p>Hosting, email delivery, Stripe Checkout and the configured AI gateway/service process information needed for their functions. Processing or transit may occur outside Canada. Stripe receives a purchase reference, Toinky user reference and bundle information; payment information entered at Stripe is handled by Stripe. Toinky keeps purchase amounts, currency, status and payment-provider references while the account is active.</p>
<p>The optional narrator downloads browser code from jsDelivr and voice/model assets from Hugging Face when enabled. These requests disclose normal connection information, including your IP address, to those services. Narrator availability is controlled by the operator; it is currently disabled. Fonts are hosted locally and the previous third-party CAPTCHA has been removed.</p>
<h2>Cookies And Browser Storage</h2>
<p>Toinky uses an essential Secure, HttpOnly session cookie and, after an unsuccessful age check, a short registration-refusal cookie. Local/session browser storage holds interface and optional assistant/narrator preferences. Optional voice-model caches may use browser storage. These are distinct from analytics. Any future non-essential analytics must be disclosed and remain off until the required opt-in is obtained.</p>
<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>The privacy retention job is designed to remove delivery logs older than 90 days, remove expired/used token and invitation records after a 30-day cleanup period, and clear all text-bearing AI log payloads older than 90 days while retaining non-identifying usage metrics. Disabled accounts that accepted this retention policy become eligible for identity erasure after <?= (int)$privacyConfig['disabled_account_days']?> days. These jobs require an operator-configured schedule; requests to remove your account identity can be made sooner through My Profile.</p>
<p>Shared fiction and game history can remain after identity erasure. Purchase/ledger totals remain without your account identity and payment-provider reference fields. Provider-held records, infrastructure logs, backups and legal obligations require a separate operational review; this policy does not promise instant removal from every backup or external provider.</p>
<p>The retention job removes session records thirty days after their stored maximum expiry or recorded revocation, and removes abandoned authenticator setup records one day after setup expiry. Enabled authenticator records remain until disabled or account identity erasure. Account deletion removes the account's session and authenticator/recovery records. Session revocation ends access on the next request; ordinary browser requests count as activity, subject to a fixed maximum lifetime.</p>
<h2>Download, Correction And Deletion</h2>
<p>My Profile provides a password-confirmed JSON download containing safe profile, membership, own character history/choices, ratings, friend relationships, invitations, purchases, occasion entries, authored-story data, media metadata, consent history, preferences and activity records. It excludes authentication secrets, unaccepted outgoing friend identities, pending email-change delivery records, and other players' private information. Request a redacted copy of personal information contained in AI text, review notes or infrastructure records through the contact address.</p>
<p>You can correct your display name and photo and request an email change by confirming your current password in My Profile. Verification at the new mailbox signs out all sessions. The previous mailbox receives a seven-day recovery link, stored only as a hash; explicit recovery restores that address, revokes sessions and authenticator/recovery codes, and requires a password reset. Mail-delivery failures or a previous address claimed by another account require support assistance. Contact us for corrections to records that are not directly editable. Identity deletion removes sign-in credentials, the account profile/photo, friend links, invitations, account-linked review text and direct attribution. Shared stories, media and game history remain without your identity or attribution, as described on the confirmation screen. Personal details embedded in shared fiction require a privacy request so we can review and redact them without exposing other people's information.</p>
<p>Super Admin ownership must be transferred before that account can be erased or disabled. This is an operational dependency, not a refusal of a privacy request. Contact us to arrange the transfer and review.</p>
<h2>Consent, Withdrawal And Requests</h2>
<p>Registration asks you to review and accept the current Terms and this notice in an unticked checkbox. Toinky records the document versions and acceptance time and asks again when versions change. This does not substitute for any separate consent required for an optional feature. Withdrawing consent in My Profile disables account use; contact us if you need access, correction, deletion or another applicable right after sign-in is disabled.</p>
<p>Send requests, questions or complaints to <a href="mailto:<?=e($privacyConfig['contact'])?>"><?=e($privacyConfig['contact'])?></a>. We verify identity using proportionate methods, avoid asking for passwords by email, protect other people's information, and explain any lawful restriction or operational dependency. Applicable rights, deadlines, exceptions and breach duties depend on the circumstances and jurisdiction.</p>
